 "text": "Skip to Main Content\n\ninfo@mazingirasafari.com\n\n+255784278205\n\nAbout Us\nContact\nFAQ's\nYour Trip\nTravel Info\nBlog\n7-Day Kilimanjaro Expedition: Machame Route Adventure\nENQUIRE NOW\n\n$2450pp\n\nBEST TIME TO TRAVEL\n\nJan- March (Less crowded)\nJun - Oct\n\nDURATION\n\n7 Days\n\nLOCATIONS\n\nMachame, Kilimanjaro Route\n\nSTARTING POINT\n\nFlight into Kilimanjaro\n\nThe Machame route on Kilimanjaro, also known as the Whiskey route, is a seven-day camping adventure offering excellent acclimatisation and an impressive range of scenery. Around 35% of climbers choose this path for its unique journey, starting at the equator and ending in the Arctic-like summit zone. Along the way, you'll traverse diverse landscapes, including lush grasslands, tropical rainforests, alpine meadows, moorlands, high deserts, and finally, the icy terrain near the peak. Each day offers a distinct ecosystem, providing a new and thrilling experience.\n\n​\n\nThe route begins on the southwest side of the mountain and circles around to the southeast, allowing climbers to spend three consecutive nights at the same altitude, significantly enhancing acclimatisation. This thoughtful design contributes to an impressive summit success rate of about 85%, making the Machame route a favourite among adventurers seeking to conquer Africa's highest peak.\n\nITINERARY\n\nDay 1\nDay 2\nDay 3\nDay 4\nDay 5\nDay 6\nDay 7\n​\n\nDay 1: Arusha - Machame Gate\n\n​\n\nDay One of your journey begins after breakfast when your guide will collect you from your previous night's accommodation or Kilimanjaro Airport. From there, you'll drive to the Mount Kilimanjaro National Park gate, passing through the picturesque Machame village on the mountain's lower slopes.\n\n​\n\nAfter completing the necessary registration formalities, you'll start your ascent through the lush rainforest. The trail can be muddy and slippery, so be prepared as you navigate the terrain. By late afternoon, you'll reach Machame Camp, where you'll enjoy a well-earned rest, a hearty dinner, and your first overnight stay on Kilimanjaro.\n\nMeal Plan\n\nBreakfast, lunch and Dinner\n\nAccomodation\n\nMachame Camp -campsite is set in a small clearing in the forest, you will see a central ranger station and a number of brick toilets and long drop latrines. The air is quite humid \n\nAltitude \n\n3000m\n\nPackage Price includes:\n\nAccommodations at mountain (Tents)\n\nProfessional and experienced mountain guides\n\nAll Park fees\n\nRescue fees\n\nAll meals while on the Mountain\n\nGuides, Porters, cook salaries and park fees\n\nQuality Mess tents with table and chairs\n\nLarge portions of fresh, healthy nutritious food\n\nPurified drinking water\n\nAirport transfers \n\nEmergency Oxygen\n\nSleeping mattress\n\nPortable toilets\n\nFirst aid kit\n\nPackage Price Does not include:\n\nTanzania Visa\n\nGratuity (tips and gifts to porters, guides and chef(s))\n\nPersonal Expenses (e.g. laundry, telephone, beverages, etc.\n\nSleeping bags (available for $35 per person throughout safari)\n\nWalking sticks (2 pairs – available for $10)\n\nTravel insurances\n\nFlights\n\nWidget Didn’t Load\nCheck your internet and refresh this page.\nIf that doesn’t work, contact us.\nRefresh this page\nContact us\n\ninfo@mazingirasafari.com\n\nuk.sales@mazingirasafari.com\n\n+255784278205 / +255767278204\n\nAccessibility Statement \n\nMazingira Eco Friendly Safari Adventure\n\nArusha \n\nP.O Box 12544\n\nStay informed, join our newsletter\n\nEnter your email here \nSubscribe\n\nMazingira Safari © 2023 | ",
